    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (7 tests, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe requirement was to return `selfLink = \"/api/owners/\" + <new owner id>` on the owner response. Owner responses (both `GET /api/owners/{id}` and `POST /api/owners`) are serialized from the generated `OwnerDto` via `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, so I added the field there rather than in any single responder:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `selfLink` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field (consistent with how the other derived fields like `displayName`, `membershipNumber`, etc. are declared).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"selfLink\", ...)` and a small single-responsibility `selfLink(Owner)` default method returning `\"/api/owners/\" + owner.getId()`, matching the existing pattern of the mapper's other derived-field helpers.\n\nNo responder or endpoint YAML needed changing \u2014 placing the logic in the mapper means every owner response gets `selfLink` for free, with no duplication. The new `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsSelfLink` passes, as do all pre-existing tests.",
